 507:main.c        **** /* Turns one "fd/bk/lt/rt <n>" into a queue entry, validating fd/bk
 508:main.c        ****    against the grid first (bounds/obstacle/diagonal-vowel) and only
 509:main.c        ****    queuing however many cells actually passed -- shared by every place
 510:main.c        ****    that builds a movement queue (top-level commands, repeat content,
 511:main.c        ****    ifelse branches, while body) so the grid check is written once.
 512:main.c        ****    lt/rt always succeed (no bounds check for turning) and update
 513:main.c        ****    heading_deg immediately. Reports a BLOCKED reason over UART_1 if
 514:main.c        ****    fd/bk couldn't fully complete. */
